'''Takia''' is an [[Austronesian languages|Austronesian]] language spoken on [[Karkar Island]], Bagabag Island, and coastal villages Megiar and Serang, [[Madang Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]]. It has been [[metatypy|syntactically restructured]] by [[Waskia language|Waskia]], a [[Papuan language]] spoken on the island.

Children are discouraged from using Takia, and it is being supplanted by [[Tok Pisin]] and English.{{Citation needed|date=February 2023}}

